-- title:
--   Relative group law from a pinned addition morphism
-- statement:
--   Let $R$ be a Noetherian integral domain and let $W$ be a Weierstrass curve over $R$ that is elliptic. Write $E = \mathrm{Proj}$ of the graded quotient of $R[X_0,X_1,X_2]$ by the homogeneous ideal generated by the Weierstrass cubic of $W$, with structure morphism $\pi =$ `projModelStrCR` to $\operatorname{Spec} R$, and for $i \in \mathrm{Fin}\,3$ let $\mathcal A_i$ denote the degree-zero homogeneous localisation of that graded ring at the class of $X_i$. Suppose given a morphism $m \colon E \times_{\pi,\pi} E \to E$ such that $m$ followed by $\pi$ equals the first pullback projection followed by $\pi$, and such that $m$ is pinned to the Lange–Ruppert law morphisms: for all $i, j \in \mathrm{Fin}\,3$ and every $l \in \mathrm{Fin}\,3 \oplus \mathrm{Fin}\,3$, the composite of the map $\operatorname{Spec}$ of the localisation of $\mathcal A_i \otimes_R \mathcal A_j$ away from `kw_lrSixU W i j l` into $\operatorname{Spec}(\mathcal A_i \otimes_R \mathcal A_j)$, the inverse of the chart isomorphism `kwProjPullbackChartIsoCR` identifying the $(i,j)$ member of the open cover `kwProjPullbackOpenCoverCR` of the pullback with that affine scheme, the open immersion of that cover member into the pullback, and $m$, equals `kw_lrSixU_toE W i j l` (the morphism into $E$ obtained from the chart tensor ring map followed by $\mathrm{Proj}.\mathrm{away}\iota$, in the $\mathrm{inl}$ case via `kw_lrChart_tensor` and in the $\mathrm{inr}$ case via `kw_lrSymChart_tensor`). Then the type `RelativeGroupLaw R` $\pi$ is nonempty: there exist operations assigning, to each scheme $T$ with a morphism $t \colon T \to \operatorname{Spec} R$, a multiplication, a unit element and an inversion on the set of morphisms $T \to E$ over $t$, satisfying associativity, both unit laws, the left inverse law, and compatibility of the multiplication with precomposition along any $\psi \colon T' \to T$ with $\psi$ followed by $t$ equal to $t'$.
--
--   This is the packaging step that turns a single global addition morphism on the projective Weierstrass model, pinned chart by chart to the six Lange–Ruppert addition law morphisms, into the group-law structure on functorial points over $\operatorname{Spec} R$. It is used by `relativeGroupLaw_nonempty_of_perChart_addMorphism_pin`, which produces such an $m$ from per-chart data; the group axioms are supplied by the companion pinning lemmas for the zero section, for negation and for associativity.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_WeierstrassProjModel_relativeGroupLaw_nonempty_of_addMorphism_sixU_pin.lean

